From 4b11a0b5447d7906cf71d0a05dcfbe1adc4f793d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: local <local@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:57:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] omamessages 0.3.0: pictures, attachments and group messages
 (MMS)

Threads show an MMS's pictures in its bubble (decoded at most 720 px on a
side, kept between refreshes, held to 240x320 by clamps) and its other
attachments as a row with the file's name and size; a tap opens either
with the desktop's app for it (gtk::FileLauncher). The parts come from the
store's parts table, files in the agent's data directory. The list says
"Picture" or "Attachment" for an MMS without text, and a failed message's
sheet gives the agent's reason ("The MMS service (mmsd-tng) isn't
running", "Too big for MMS: ...").

The attach button works: a file dialog with pictures first, several
files at once, a preview strip above the composer with a button to take
each out again. With attachments the message goes through omatel 0.3's
SendToConversationWithAttachments; text alone keeps the 0.2 call, so an
older agent still sends it. MmsUnavailable leaves the message as "Not
sent" for Retry and says so; other failures put text and files back.

Group conversations are real: sms: links with several recipients open
one (no more "writing to the first number"), and the new-message page
puts several people together (the + on a suggestion, chips that take a
person out, Start). A group's thread shows "N people", who wrote each
incoming run, and no Call button; its messages go as MMS (the agent's
choice), so the composer stops counting SMS parts.

The MMS settings group now edits mmsd-tng's MMSC, MMS proxy and MMS APN
(src/mmsconfig.rs). mmsd-tng keeps them in ~/.mms/modemmanager/mms
([Modem Manager] CarrierMMSC, CarrierMMSProxy, MMS_APN; empty is
http://mms.invalid for the MMSC and NULL for the others) and writes its
copy back when it stops, so while it runs the change goes through its
org.ofono.mms.ModemManager.ChangeSettings (applies at once, mmsd-tng
saves the file, then ProcessMessageQueue), and while it doesn't, into the
file, edited in place (one line changes; comments, other keys and groups
stay). If a running mmsd-tng refuses, it is stopped, the file written and
it is started again (systemctl --user, mmsd-tng.service).

Script steps `attach PATH` and `add NUMBER` for screenshots. Tests for the
settings file (placeholders, in-place edits, new groups, escapes, mode
0600), attachment stand-ins and sizes.

Cargo.toml patches omatel's crates to ../omatel until omatel 0.3.0 is
tagged; then the tag bump replaces the patch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
